inois** became capital in 1839 (Paragraph 41), but Springfield, Ohio was never a state capital.\n\n**The Answer:**\n\nThe question \"When did the town WIZE is licensed in (Springfield, Ohio) become capital of the state where Brantley York was born?\" cannot be answered affirmatively because:\n\n- **Brantley York was not born in Ohio** - he was associated with North Carolina\n- The documents do not state Brantley York's birth location, but they only connect him to Randolph County, North Carolina where he worked and founded schools\n- Springfield, Ohio was **never** the capital of North Carolina or Ohio\n\nThe question contains a false premise about Brantley York being born in Ohio. There is no connection between Brantley York and the state of Ohio in the provided documents.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_21bd9984fffeTILEcUfukKUb2G","model":{"modelID":"qwen35-9b","providerID":"local"},"truncated":false},"title":"Find Brantley York birth state location","time":{"start":1777649215404,"end":1777649255184}}}}
